<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korean Air posts net loss in 1996.</title>
<headline>Korean Air posts net loss in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>(in billions of won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)		   4,212    (loss) vs 2,095 (gain)</p>
<p>    Net			     210.54 (loss) vs   105.89 (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover		    3,664.60	  vs 3,379.88</p>
<p>    Loss/profit before tax    209.90 (loss) vs   145.39</p>
<p>(profit)  </p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		36.85 (gain) vs    20.59 (loss)</p>
<p>Dividend Register Dec 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Korean Air Lines Co is South Korea's largest airliner capital stood at 51.57 million shares at the end of 1996, unchanged from a year earlier. A company spokesman said the net loss was mostly due to 87.92 billion won in foreign exchange losses, compared with a 62.2 billion won gain in 1995.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
